# GitHub-to-AAP integration pattern

This project intentionally routes GitHub automation through Event-Driven
Ansible rather than AAP's native per-job-template webhooks, and never
stores a static GitHub PAT. Preserve this pattern in any related change:

- **Single entry point**: GitHub `pull_request`/`push` events must go to
  one EDA Event Stream, which forwards to the Rulebook Activation running
  `rulebooks/lightwell_webhook.yml`. That rulebook decides which job
  template(s) to launch (`run_job_template`) and with which extra vars
  (`app_git_sha`, `github_repo_full_name`, etc.). Do not configure a
  webhook directly on an AAP job template.
- **One rule per event**: The rulebook has a separate rule per event
  (PR build & test, demo reset, deploy prod), each launching the
  matching job template (`Lightwell // Build & Test`,
  `Lightwell // Deploy Prod`).
- **No static GitHub tokens**: Authenticate to GitHub's API using a token
  minted on demand from a GitHub App installation via the
  `GitHub App Installation Access Token Lookup` credential (chained into a
  `GitHub Status Token`-type credential). Never add a plain GitHub PAT as
  a credential or extra var.
- **Status reporting is explicit**: Because job templates no longer have a
  native webhook receiver, they must call the
  `demo.lightwell.report_status` role in `pre_tasks`/`post_tasks` to post
  `pending`/`success`/`failure` commit statuses back to GitHub. Keep this
  role's variables (`github_token`, `github_repo_full_name`, `app_git_sha`,
  `github_status_state`, `github_status_description`) intact and tolerant
  of manual (non-EDA) launches by not failing when they're undefined. The
  status context (`ci/lightwell-java-{{ app_environment }}`) uniquely
  identifies this app's checks in branch protection.
- **Keep `docs/aap-setup.md` in sync**: If you change the Event Stream,
  GitHub App, rulebook conditions, or `report_status` role, update
  `docs/aap-setup.md` (and the README's architecture diagram/pipeline
  walkthrough) so the setup guide matches the actual wiring.

Consider these rules if they affect your changes.
